      "text": "To find the smallest positive value of \\( x \\) such that \\( x + 5678 \\) results in a palindrome, we need to iterate through positive integers and check for each one whether \\( x + 5678 \\) is a palindrome. A palindrome is a number that reads the same backward as forward.\n\nWe can write a function to check if a number is a palindrome and then iterate through positive integers until we find the smallest \\( x \\). Here is the step-by-step process:\n\n1. Define a function to check if a number is a palindrome.\n2. Iterate through positive integers and check if adding 5678 to each integer results in a palindrome.\n3. Return the smallest positive integer \\( x \\) for which \\( x + 5678 \\) is a palindrome.\n\nLet's write the Python code to solve this problem.\n```python\ndef is_palindrome(n):\r\n    return str(n) == str(n)[::-1]\r\n\r\nx = 1\r\nwhile True:\r\n    if is_palindrome(x + 5678):\r\n        break\r\n    x += 1\r\n\r\nprint(x)\n```\n```output\n8005\n```\nThe smallest positive value of \\( x \\) such that \\( x + 5678 \\) results in a palindrome is \\(\\boxed{8005}\\).",
